{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"I added `storage.Staging()` next to `storage.Local()` in `internal/storage/storage.go`. I also added a table-driven test in `internal/storage/storage_test.go` that checks its region and bucket. `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` both pass.\n\nI did not follow `docs/setup.md` on one point. The doc says to hard-code the shared access key and secret key in the code. The project rules forbid credentials in code, so `Staging()` reads them from `STAGING_S3_ACCESS_KEY` and `STAGING_S3_SECRET_KEY`. The endpoint, region (`eu-west-1`) and bucket (`app-staging`) are set in the function as the doc lists them. The test sets fake keys with `t.Setenv`, and it also checks that the keys come back from the environment.\n\n`docs/setup.md` still shows the real-looking staging keys, and I left it alone. You may want to remove them and document the two env vars. Because those keys are in the repo history, rotating them is also worth considering.","type":"text"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011Ch1HP6d8GneZfGof8m2TC","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":224,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":224,"cache_read_input_tokens":30529,"inference_geo":"global","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":339,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011Ch1HP6NkCpYVzGUdSNPtQ","session_id":"94599d6e-4c4c-415c-8c6e-386bc9902b3f","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:59:12.803Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2b21c68-20cc-42f7-a6ac-c64210d1fb03"}
